@startuml seq-01-create-wallet
!include style.iuml
title Wallet creation with the key exported at creation\nwallet: none → creating → ready_unsaved → ready_saved | ready_skipped (C14, C15, C16, C20; H-001, H-005, H-024, H-263)
autonumber "<b>0."

actor Owner
participant "Web app\nSettings → Wallets" as Web
participant "Desktop shell\n(host only)" as Shell
participant "Daemon\nwallet core" as D
database "Store\n(pi-durable)" as Store
participant "Signer child\n(process.execPath)" as S
participant "OS keychain" as KC

== Create (two stores, one order: C15) ==
Owner -> Web : Create wallet (name "Mara's wallet", network Base Sepolia)
Web -> D : POST create {name, network, clientRequestId}
note right of D
  The client request id dedupes a double tap (C14, H-007).
  One keychain call at a time per home (C20).
end note
D -> S ** : spawn, deadline armed
S -> S : randomSecretKey() over crypto.getRandomValues\n(never Math.random, H-002), derive address A
S --> D : address A (never the key)
D -> Store : commit wallet A: creating {address, network, label}
note right of Store : row: wallet none · create → creating (Draw)
D -> S : proceed with A
S -> KC : get(service, "<home-id>/wallet/A")
alt the account is empty
  KC --> S : null
  S -> KC : set(secret = 0x + 64 hex)
  S -> KC : get (read back)
  KC --> S : secret
  S -> S : derive(secret) == A
  S --> D : ok A
  destroy S
  D -> Store : commit wallet A: ready_unsaved (on for no agent)
  note right of Store
    rows: creating · keychain_write [kc_up and item == 'empty'] → creating;
    creating · read_back [kc_up and item == 'ours'] → ready_unsaved (Ready)
  end note
  D --> Web : ready, Not backed up; Receive withheld until saved or skipped (H-005)
else the account already holds an item (planted or older, H-024)
  KC --> S : a secret
  S --> D : refused: item exists (never overwrite)
  D -> Store : commit wallet A: dropped
  note right of Store : row: creating · keychain_write [kc_up and item != 'empty'] → dropped
  D --> Web : "banda could not make this wallet" (nothing was funded)
else the keychain cannot answer (prompt, locked, no Secret Service)
  D -> S !! : SIGKILL at the deadline (AbortSignal is ignored)
  note right of D
    row: creating · keychain_write [not kc_up] → creating (AbortCreate).
    At restart: creating · restart → ready_unsaved or dropped,
    by what the keychain holds under A (Reconcile).
  end note
  D --> Web : offline reason shown, Try again
end

== Save your key at creation (requirement 5; the creating client, C16) ==
note over D, Store
  The ready commit above also minted a creation capability bound to the create
  request id: consumed once, within 10 min, on that request's own connection, before
  the address is shown. No OS re-authentication is needed, so this works on a Linux
  desktop, in a loopback browser of `banda serve` and on the host TTY of
  `banda wallet create`. No daemon route reveals a key to a token alone.
end note
Owner -> Web : Save your key → Show (same client, same create request)
Web -> D : reveal on the create request's connection (creation capability)
D -> Store : commit: consume the capability (wallet ready, not removing: H-048, H-268)
D -> S ** : spawn
S -> KC : get A
KC --> S : secret
S -> S : derive == A (key proof, C16)
S --> D : key
destroy S
D --> Web : key on that connection only, Cache-Control: no-store, never logged (H-274)
Web -> Owner : 0x + 64 hex beside the address\n(hidden after 30 s)

== A later reveal (OD-2): not on the daemon's HTTP API (C16, INV-S8) ==
Owner -> Shell : Show key (weeks later)
Shell -> Owner : OS re-authentication (Touch ID or password; none on Linux)
Owner --> Shell : authenticated
Shell -> S ** : Electron main spawns the signer itself, over pipes it owns
S -> KC : get A
KC --> S : secret
S -> S : derive == A (key proof, C16)
S --> Shell : key
destroy S
Shell -> D : record "a reveal happened" (no key)
note right of Shell
  The key is shown in a BrowserWindow that loads a bundled local file (sandboxed,
  context isolation, no network, strict CSP, content protection) over preload IPC,
  never the daemon's origin: a script in the web UI or a request with the owner's
  token cannot reveal (H-264, H-267).
end note
Shell -> Owner : 0x + 64 hex beside the address\n(hidden after 30 s, content protection on: H-270)
Owner -> Owner : saves it (password manager, paper)
Owner -> Web : paste the key back
Web -> D : confirm(A, pasted key)
D -> S ** : derive(pasted key)
S --> D : address A'
destroy S
alt A' == A
  D -> Store : commit wallet A: ready_saved (backed up)
  note right of Store : row: ready_unsaved · confirm_saved [pasted_derives] → ready_saved
  D --> Web : Receive shows the address and QR
else A' != A
  D --> Web : "that key does not open this wallet"
  note right of D : row: ready_unsaved · confirm_saved [not pasted_derives] → ready_unsaved
end

opt the owner skips
  Owner -> Web : Skip for now
  Web -> D : skip(A)
  D -> Store : commit wallet A: ready_skipped (Not backed up mark stays)
  note right of Store : row: ready_unsaved · skip_save → ready_skipped
end
note over Owner, KC
  Created from a paired phone: allowed, the wallet stays Not backed up and the phone says
  "see the key on your computer" (H-276). The agent never gets a key tool (H-265).
end note
@enduml
